Found during k100 (worker, reproduced). Inside a skill directory, SKILL.md beside SKILL.md.njk (or any companion f beside f.njk) both render to the same install path: the template silently wins, while the catalog shows the plain file's description; no warning. Expected: consistent with k100 – an error of that skill (available shows it, install refuses, sync warns and keeps an installed copy), naming both files. Document in spec §4.1 next to the k100 paragraph.

2026-09-27 04:35 Reproduced (worker): skills/x/{SKILL.md,SKILL.md.njk,scripts/x.sh,scripts/x.sh.njk} scans as one skill, description 'plain' (SKILL.md, skillFile() tries it first), no error; render.build() iterates the sorted files, so the .njk (later) overwrites the plain file at the same install path for both SKILL.md and scripts/x.sh. Cause: scan/pluginSkills/claudeItem build a skill item from walkFiles() without checking for install-path collisions.

2026-09-27 04:38 Decisions (worker): (1) every clashing pair is named, in sorted order, joined by '; ' (e.g. 'both skills/x/SKILL.md and skills/x/SKILL.md.njk exist; both skills/x/a.sh and skills/x/a.sh.njk exist'), paths relative to the source like k100 – one fix round for the author. (2) A clash is by install path: plain f beside f.njk; f.njk beside f.njk.njk is NOT a clash (they install as f and f.njk). (3) Description: omitted while SKILL.md itself is in a pair (ambiguous, as k100's agent/rule); kept when only a companion clashes (SKILL.md is unambiguous). (4) .claude/: a skill's inner clash IS an error there too (maintainer's lean) – inside one skill dir there is no 'which item wins' question, only an ambiguous file; it stays best effort in that it never fails the scan. k100's silent first-wins for .claude/ agents/rules is unchanged. A broken published skill still counts as found, so a .claude/ skill of that name does not step in. Fix is one helper skillItem() in src/catalog.ts used by scan (skills/), pluginSkills and claudeItem; engine/commands/cli unchanged (k100 wiring). Red tests confirmed first (4/4 failed for the card's reason).

